WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:02.547
Rather than wait for death

00:02.680 --> 00:04.347
Better to take the initiative

00:04.480 --> 00:05.520
Prepare troops, exit the city

00:05.680 --> 00:07.080
Yes

00:26.400 --> 00:27.600
General

00:27.680 --> 00:28.480
General

00:28.560 --> 00:29.960
General's calculations are flawless

00:30.200 --> 00:31.600
They've left the city

00:32.960 --> 00:34.160
Brothers

00:34.240 --> 00:35.120
Mount up

00:35.240 --> 00:35.920
I'll lead you

00:36.000 --> 00:37.480
To take the city today

00:37.560 --> 00:38.720
Yes

00:48.500 --> 00:54.000
You dispatched most of the Yiyang garrison to mount a surprise raid on the Wunu rear, never expecting to be ambushed on your flank by Shi Lang's elite cavalry.

00:54.500 --> 01:02.000
With just a single charge, the ranks of two thousand soldiers were pierced through by iron cavalry. The Yiyang Army retreated in panic as Shi Lang pursued relentlessly, reaping heads like mowing wheat.

01:02.500 --> 01:10.000
Witnessing this slaughter and pursuit, the confidence of the defenders within the city collapsed completely. Yiyang, which had previously held out for six days, fell in less than a single shichen.

01:10.500 --> 01:18.500
In the eleventh year of Yuankang, Shi Lang slew King of Jin Sikong Yao, laughing: "Great Xuan shall perish by my hands." He then hung his severed head from his horse as a trophy.

